{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7c9e1a2b-4d3f-4a80-9c12-5e6f7a8b9c0d",
    "name": "AirPay Payment Gateway",
    "description": "Django REST API for AirPay.\n\n**Suggested order**\n\n1. Health \u2192 Register \u2192 Login (saves JWT tokens)\n2. Get / Update me\n3. Create API key (saves `api_key`)\n4. Add a bank account (saves `bank_account_id`)\n5. Create a **card** transaction with `X-API-Key` (credits **unsettled** only on SUCCESS). The card service must be running on port 8001.\n6. Get balance \u2192 Settle (choose a bank account and an amount; moves unsettled to **settled**)\n7. Request a payout (debits settled, mock bank transfer)\n8. Refunds: refund part of the card transaction, then the rest (JWT; commission is returned in proportion). Run these before paying out, or the money may be gone.\n9. Payments Whoami\n10. Refresh token\n11. Revoke API key and Logout last \u2014 they are destructive\n\nDashboard endpoints send `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}`. Transactions and Whoami send `X-API-Key: {{api_key}}`.\n\nUPI and netbanking start as PENDING and do not credit the wallet until you poll Get transaction after they succeed.\n\nA payout to an account number ending in `0000` fails and the settled balance is restored. A refund ending in 99 paise is declined by the mock bank and moves no money.\n\nRegister returns 400 if `{{email}}` is already taken \u2014 skip to Login.\nStart the app with `uv run python manage.py runserver 8000`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Check health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('gateway is up', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/health",
            "description": "Liveness and readiness. Returns 200 when the database answers `SELECT 1`, otherwise 503. No login."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customer_id', body.id);",
                  "  pm.test('signed up', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.email).to.eql(pm.environment.get('email'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "  });",
                  "} else if (pm.response.code === 400) {",
                  "  pm.test('email already registered \u2014 skip to Login', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().success).to.eql(false);",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"first_name\": \"{{first_name}}\",\n  \"last_name\": \"{{last_name}}\",\n  \"company_name\": \"{{company_name}}\",\n  \"company_address\": \"{{company_address}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers",
            "description": "Create a customer. Password must pass Django's validators (length, not common, not all digits, not too similar to the name or email). 400 if the email is already taken."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('access', 'refresh');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('access_token', body.access);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('refresh_token', body.refresh);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "description": "Exchange email and password for an access token (15 minutes) and a refresh token (7 days). Saves both into the environment. A wrong password and an unknown email return the same 401."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh tokens",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rotated the pair', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('access', 'refresh');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('access_token', body.access);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('refresh_token', body.refresh);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
            "description": "Send the current refresh token. The response has a new access token and a new refresh token. The one you sent is revoked, so keep the new one. Reusing the old one returns 401."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('refresh token revoked', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('refresh_token');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
            "description": "Revokes the refresh token (204). An access token already issued keeps working until it expires. Run this last if you still need the JWT for other requests."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Customers",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns this customer', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.email).to.eql(pm.environment.get('email'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customer_id', body.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me",
            "description": "The logged-in customer. Needs `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('profile updated', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().company_name).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"{{first_name}}\",\n  \"last_name\": \"{{last_name}}\",\n  \"company_name\": \"{{company_name}}\",\n  \"company_address\": \"{{company_address}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me",
            "description": "Change `first_name`, `last_name`, `company_name`, `company_address`. Email, password, id and staff flags in the body are ignored. PUT and DELETE are not allowed."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "API keys",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create API key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const expires = new Date();",
                  "expires.setUTCDate(expires.getUTCDate() + 30);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('api_key_expires_at', expires.toISOString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('key issued once', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.key).to.match(/^apk_/);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('active');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('api_key', body.key);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('api_key_id', body.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman\",\n  \"expires_at\": \"{{api_key_expires_at}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me/api-keys",
            "description": "Needs a JWT. `expires_at` is required, must be in the future, and at most 365 days away. The pre-request script sets it to 30 days from now.\n\nThe secret is in `key` and is shown this once. The test script saves it as `{{api_key}}`. Store it; list and get never return it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List API keys",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('secrets are not listed', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const keys = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(keys).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  keys.forEach(function (k) {",
                  "    pm.expect(k).to.not.have.property('key');",
                  "    pm.expect(k).to.not.have.property('secret_hash');",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me/api-keys",
            "description": "Every key this customer holds. Use `prefix` and `last_four` to recognise one. The secret is never included."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get API key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('one key, no secret', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('api_key_id'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('key');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me/api-keys/{{api_key_id}}",
            "description": "One of your keys. Another customer's id is a 404. Run Create API key first so `{{api_key_id}}` is set."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Revoke API key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('revoked', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me/api-keys/{{api_key_id}}",
            "description": "The key stops working at once. Idempotent: revoking twice is still 204. Run Payments Whoami before this if you want to see a working key."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Transactions",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create card transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "postman-pay-1"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/transactions",
            "description": "API key, not JWT. Routes to the card service. Credits **unsettled** only when status is SUCCESS. Needs the card service on port 8001. Visa 4111111111111111 is approved.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"method\": \"CARD\",\n  \"amount\": \"1500.50\",\n  \"currency\": \"INR\",\n  \"reference\": \"order_1001\",\n  \"card\": {\n    \"card_type\": \"credit\",\n    \"number\": \"4111111111111111\",\n    \"expiry_month\": 12,\n    \"expiry_year\": 2030,\n    \"cvv\": \"123\",\n    \"holder_name\": \"Jane Doe\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('card transaction stored', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.environment.set('transaction_id', body.id);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.instrument).to.not.have.property('number');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create UPI transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/transactions",
            "description": "Starts a UPI collect. Status is PENDING and the wallet is not credited until you poll Get transaction after the payer approves. Needs the UPI service on port 8003.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"method\": \"UPI\",\n  \"amount\": \"1500.50\",\n  \"payer_vpa\": \"jane.doe@okaxis\",\n  \"description\": \"Order 1001\",\n  \"reference\": \"order_1001\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('transaction_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create netbanking transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/transactions",
            "description": "Starts netbanking and returns redirect_url. Open that URL, log in at the bank page, then poll Get transaction. Needs the netbanking service on port 8002.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"method\": \"NETBANKING\",\n  \"amount\": \"1500.50\",\n  \"bank_code\": \"HDFC\",\n  \"return_url\": \"https://shop.example.com/return\",\n  \"reference\": \"order_1001\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('transaction_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Whoami",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('API key accepted', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.email).to.eql(pm.environment.get('email'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.api_key_id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('api_key_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments/whoami",
            "description": "Confirms the API key. A JWT is not accepted here (`Authorization: Api-Key {{api_key}}` also works). Create an API key first. The same header is used on /api/v1/transactions."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/transactions/{{transaction_id}}",
            "description": "If the transaction is still PENDING, AirPay asks the rail again and credits the wallet if it succeeded.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('found', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Bank accounts",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Add bank account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/customers/me/bank-accounts",
            "description": "Needs a JWT. The full account number is shown only in the request. List and get return the last four digits.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
